{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 1, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-3520", :event/action "Added Germany (:DEU) as a 4th jurisdiction to gas.facts/catalog (was JPN/USA/GBR). Every :spec-basis cites a real, WebFetch-verified section of the Energiewirtschaftsgesetz (EnWG), published at gesetze-im-internet.de (Federal Ministry of Justice), enforced by the Bundesnetzagentur: §18 (Allgemeine Anschlusspflicht) + §36 (Grundversorgungspflicht) for the connection/basic-supply-eligibility requirement, §40a (Verbrauchsermittlung für Energierechnungen) for meter/consumption measurement, §40 for billing-disclosure content, §41g for payment-delinquency supply suspension. Added a germany-jurisdiction-requirements test mirroring the existing japan-jurisdiction-requirements one.", :event/verification "clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 21 tests / 66 assertions, 0 failures both times (new test counted in the after total). Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-3520-deu-gas-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3520/merges, commit e8964cb030a649df4ca057855e36f9e140ec0e21) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 9f2c825a013757f86363451a12c6426cfe5b49af -> e8964cb030a649df4ca057855e36f9e140ec0e21 via nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-isic-3520 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "Manually inspected ~6 of the 70 isic repos flagged real-world-ingest-gap? with an existing facts.cljc before picking isic-3520. cloud-itonami-isic-0111 (cerealops) and its whole cerealops/cattleops-derived agriculture+food+manufacturing sibling family (0112-0170, 1010-1104, etc, roughly 60+ of the 70) have a facts.cljc that is legitimately internal reference data (procurement cost thresholds, crop/product taxonomy) with no external-citation concept in that domain -- NOT a real gap, a metric false-positive. Not touched. Logged here so a future iteration does not re-investigate this family from scratch.", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready? (stub-scaffold) repo attempted -- the owner's other axis. Deferred to iteration 2: iteration 1's real per-repo effort (shape classification + WebFetch research + edit + test + full git-flow land) ran long enough that also rushing a from-zero ~1500-line actor scaffold in the same iteration would have meant cutting corners, which this loop's guardrails forbid. The isco family (216/216 flagged gap) is architecturally out of scope until a separate design decision on whether an external-citation concept belongs in its 4-file {governor,actor,advisor,store}.cljc shape -- explicitly not attempted, see ADR-2607211900.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 1, :event/at "2026-07-21T05:00:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 2, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-bgr", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Bulgaria (BGR) from a pure blueprint-only stub (zero prior src/test files). Delegated the implementation to a background agent (isolated /tmp clone, never touched the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/ checkout or main), briefed to mirror cloud-itonami-iso3166-jpn/-deu's exact architecture (marketentry.{facts,governor,phase,sim,operation,registry,store,marketentryllm}.cljc + a separate statute/facts.cljc) while researching and WebFetch-verifying every Bulgaria-specific citation for real, never copying JPN's Japan-specific business content. Delivered: marketentry.facts (BGR public-procurement market-entry: CAIS EOP/ЦАИС ЕОП platform under ЗОП Art. 39a, Commercial Register/ЕИК under Art. 60(1), honestly-scoped rep-spec-basis limited to what ЗОП Art. 54(2)-(3) actually supports rather than a stronger unverifiable claim) + statute.facts (Commerce Act, Labour Code, Personal Data Protection Act, each citing the specific Bulgarian government body hosting that law's text, since Bulgaria has no single consolidated-law portal like JPN's e-gov.go.jp or DEU's gesetze-im-internet.de) + a genuinely new governor check (flagship for the iso3166 family, grep-verified absent elsewhere at build time): independently recomputing whether declared tax/social-security arrears exceed ЗОП Art. 54(5)'s de-minimis carve-out (1% of annual turnover, capped at BGN 50,000) rather than trusting a boolean flag. Also fixed a pre-existing copy-paste bug (leftover Cambodia/cloud-itonami-iso3166-khm text in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md, unrelated to this task but found during the work).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) spot-checked 6 of the citation URLs live via curl/WebFetch myself (cpdp.bg personal-data-protection-act page, justice.government.bg Commerce Act PDF + Labour Code page, www2.aop.bg Public Procurement Act PDF, eop.bg, portal.registryagency.bg) -- all real, all HTTP 200, content matching the claims; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked orgs/kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain} for :local/root resolution) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 35 tests / 114 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's reported numbers exactly; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 9 warnings, matching exactly; (4) confirmed via git diff that the Cambodia-text fix claim was real and no khm/Cambodia references remained; (5) confirmed main was untouched by the agent (compare API + git log) before merging myself. Landed via the agent's pushed branch itonami-loop/bgr-marketentry-scaffold -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-bgr/merges, commit 9af257edc546447cfa2108564498e1d97b48d22b) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced cf7f00908a21 -> 9af257edc546 via nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-iso3166-bgr (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready, not real-world-ingest-gap).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "Did not attempt a second stub repo this iteration -- one full from-zero actor scaffold (marketentry + statute, ~2025 lines across 25 files, real per-country legal research) is a substantial, non-trivial unit of work on its own; per this loop's guardrails, delegating it to a background agent and then genuinely independently re-verifying the result (not just trusting the agent's report) is itself the bulk of an iteration's real effort. Batch size for prod-ready stub-scaffolds should likely stay at 1/iteration given this observed cost, distinct from the smaller real-world-ingest-gap axis (iteration 1) which can plausibly sustain the owner's original 3-5/iteration estimate for citation-only additions to an already-correctly-shaped facts.cljc.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 2, :event/at "2026-07-21T05:26:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 3, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-3530", :event/action "Added France (:FRA) as a 4th jurisdiction to steam.facts/catalog (was JPN/USA/GBR), the steam/chilled-water sibling of iteration 1's isic-3520 gas.facts. France's réseaux de chaleur/froid regime is genuinely differently-shaped from the other jurisdictions' customer-facing metering/disclosure rules -- it regulates mandatory CONNECTION to classified networks, not per-customer metering -- so the entry uses honestly-named requirement keys (:mandatory-connection, :network-classification-disclosure) rather than force-fitting JPN/USA/GBR's :customer-verification/:thermal-meter-inspection shape. Every citation independently WebFetch-verified against legifrance.gouv.fr (France's official law portal), Code de l'énergie Book VII Title I Chapter II: L712-2+L712-3 (priority development zones + mandatory connection for >30kW installations), L712-1 (energy audit + financial-viability assessment for classified networks), L712-5 (EUR 300,000 fine for non-compliance, kept under its own :non-compliance-with-connection-obligation key rather than folded into :payment-delinquency since it is a penalty on the building owner, not an operator-exercised supply-suspension power -- and a test explicitly asserts :payment-delinquency returns false for :FRA rather than silently omitting the check).", :event/verification "clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 22 tests / 63 assertions, 0 failures both times. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-3530-fra-steam-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3530/merges, commit 6f284d9e30a15be0ded3c753022732515b8421c4) -> branch deleted.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None new this iteration (isic-3530 was pre-selected as a same-family sibling of isic-3520, already confirmed genuinely regulatory-citation-shaped, not re-derived from scratch).", :event/operational-note "This iteration ran in an isolated sibling git worktree (/tmp/root-worktrees/<name>, outside the superproject root) per the updated skill `git-operations` guidance (superproject root checkout is now 統合・閲覧専用 -- 直接 commit/branch しない) and per ADR-2607211600 (shallow depth-1 retired repo-wide 2026-07-21; the superproject clone in this session was still shallow and needed `git fetch --unshallow` before merges stopped false-positiving as 'unrelated histories'). Found and worked around a real limitation while doing so: `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry <name>` resolves a pin via `(or (working-head path) (:revision existing))`, i.e. it reads the LOCAL child-repo checkout under orgs/<org>/<repo> for the live HEAD and only falls back to the existing (stale) west.yml value when that local checkout is absent -- which it always is in an ad hoc worktree that hasn't run `west update`, so every attempt from the worktree silently kept writing the OLD pin. Worked around by querying the live default-branch HEAD directly via `gh api repos/<org>/<repo>/branches/main -q .commit.sha` and hand-editing just that one west.yml line, then independently confirming via `nbb scripts/verify-west-pins.cljs --only <name>` (reported a clean fast-forward) rather than trusting the generator script's output blindly. Future iterations working from an isolated worktree should expect this and verify the same way, or run `west init -l manifest && west update --fetch smart <repo>` inside the worktree first so `working-head` has something real to read.", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready? (stub-scaffold) repo attempted this iteration either (axis stayed on real-world-ingest-gap, continuing iteration 1's smaller-batch-capable axis rather than alternating strictly one-for-one with iteration 2's heavier stub-scaffold axis).", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 3, :event/at "2026-07-21T06:45:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 4, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-aze", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Azerbaijan (AZE) from a pure blueprint-only stub, same pattern as iteration 2 (Bulgaria): delegated implementation to a background agent (isolated /tmp clone, never touched the shared checkout or main), briefed to mirror the JPN/DEU/BGR architecture while genuinely researching every Azerbaijan-specific citation. Delivered: marketentry.facts (etender.gov.az Unified Internet Portal for State Procurement under Law No. 988-VIQ; State Tax Service VÖEN/corporate-registration; a genuinely new 'unreliable-supplier registry' flagship check per Cabinet of Ministers Decision No. 492; explicitly verified, not assumed, that ASAN xidmət is a real intake channel but not the registering authority itself) + statute.facts (Labour Code, Personal Data Law, Civil Code) + honest scope-narrowing (rep-spec-basis returns nil for AZE -- found evidence of foreign-representative-office registration generally but not a verified procurement-specific resident-representative mandate, so it was not claimed). Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template bug in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md that iteration 2 found in Bulgaria's repo.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session: (1) spot-checked citation URLs live -- taxes.gov.az, competition.gov.az (unreliable-supplier page), asan.gov.az all returned real HTTP 200 content matching the claims; etender.gov.az timed out at the TCP level from this environment (both curl and WebFetch), so its liveness was instead corroborated via WebSearch against 3 independent secondary sources (a tender-listing site, a news article, and competition.gov.az's own English page, which shares the same contact email domain) rather than left unverified; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked orgs/kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 34 tests / 108 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 9 warnings, matching exactly; (4) confirmed no khm/Cambodia references remained; (5) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-aze checkout was untouched before merging. Landed via server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-aze/merges, commit ac694148ece63728ef552e742ae02d8cb6534387) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 6c081cf55aec -> ac694148ece6, done from an isolated worktree via direct GitHub-API SHA query + hand-edit + verify-west-pins cross-check per the workaround iteration 3 documented (gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cannot see a live local checkout from an ad hoc worktree and silently keeps the stale pin).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo attempted this iteration -- axis alternation is now 2 prod-ready / 2 real-world-ingest-gap across 4 iterations, roughly balanced per the owner's original interleaving instruction.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 4, :event/at "2026-07-21T07:05:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 5, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-alb", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Albania (ALB) from a pure blueprint-only stub, same pattern as iterations 2/4. Delivered: marketentry.facts (Agjencia e Prokurimit Publik / APP electronic procurement system under Ligji Nr. 162/2020 'Për Prokurimin Publik' Neni 4/23/56; explicitly investigated rather than assumed the QKB-vs-tax-authority NUIS question -- confirmed via the tax authority's OWN site that QKB generates the NUIS at registration and DPT is only notified afterward, so QKB is cited as corporate-number-owner-authority, not DPT; a flat ALL 10,000 tax-arrears de-minimis flagship check under Neni 76(2)(c), a third distinct check shape for this family after Bulgaria's turnover-scaled formula and Azerbaijan's boolean registry membership) + statute.facts (confirmed Albania has a standalone Commercial Companies Law (Ligji Nr. 9901/2008) separate from its Civil Code, unlike Azerbaijan where commerce law lives inside the Civil Code -- verified by research rather than assumed by analogy) + honest scope-narrowing (rep-spec-basis is real but narrow, a conviction-based personal-exclusion extension per Neni 76(1), not a resident-representative mandate; APP's real Neni 78 'excluded economic operators' registry was found and deliberately left unimplemented as a second check to avoid scope-padding).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session: (1) spot-checked all 3 core citation URLs live (app.gov.al, app.gov.al/legislation/public-procurement/law/, qkb.gov.al) -- all HTTP 200; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked orgs/kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 35 tests / 112 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 9 warnings, matching exactly; (4) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-alb checkout was untouched before merging. Landed via server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-alb/merges, commit cb8e158ba7dd8291b29381b1d7c13f7df7826723) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 03a3799a1469 -> cb8e158ba7dd, done from an isolated worktree via direct GitHub-API SHA query + hand-edit + verify-west-pins cross-check.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "Two more real-world-ingest-gap metric false positives found while scouting this iteration's OTHER axis before settling on another prod-ready target: cloud-itonami-isic-8030 (private investigation) has a facts.cljc that is a flat, deliberately US-scoped licensing-QUALIFICATION-CLASS catalog (state PI license, FCRA cert, etc), not a per-jurisdiction citation table -- adding a country entry would misuse the shape. cloud-itonami-isic-791 (travel agency) has a facts.cljc that is a pure booking/client data-integrity-check helper with no citation concept at all. Neither touched; logged so a future iteration does not re-investigate. Also confirmed a prior finding still holds: isic-3520/isic-3530 (iterations 1/3) still show real-world-ingest-gap? true in a freshly-regenerated manifest/itonami-fleet-audit.edn, NOT because the fix regressed but because gas.facts/steam.facts cite statutes by name+section text, never a literal https:// URL -- the metric's known https?://-counting blind spot (documented in ADR-2607211900) correctly does not detect them as fixed even though they are. Not a bug to chase this iteration; a reminder that this metric needs the reader's own judgment, not blind trust, exactly as designed.", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration (2 more screened-out false positives instead) -- axis alternation is now 3 prod-ready / 2 real-world-ingest-gap across 5 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 5, :event/at "2026-07-21T08:50:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 6, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1910", :event/action "Added South Korea (:KOR) as a 4th jurisdiction to coke.facts/catalog (was JPN/USA/GBR), the coke-oven-manufacturing sibling of the isic-3520/3530 utility-safety family. Before picking a target, systematically classified all 70 isic repos flagged real-world-ingest-gap? with an existing facts.cljc by grepping each for a :spec-basis key (the signature of the genuine per-jurisdiction citation shape gas.facts/steam.facts/coke.facts share) -- only 8 of 70 matched, 2 of which (isic-3520/3530) were already fixed in iterations 1/3, leaving 6 genuine new candidates (isic-1410/1420/1430/1512/1910/3020) instead of the mostly-false-positive agriculture/food/manufacturing/qualification-class/data-helper shapes sampled in prior iterations. Citations: emissions-monitoring under the Clean Air Conservation Act (대기환경보전법) Art. 23 (permit/reporting for emission-facility installation); worker-safety under the Occupational Safety and Health Act (산업안전보건법) Art. 80 (hazardous-machinery protective measures) + Art. 36 (risk assessment covering raw materials/gas/steam/dust -- directly on point for coke-oven operations). No raw-material-verification or byproduct-handling entry made for KOR -- honestly narrower than JPN/USA/GBR since this iteration did not find/verify a citation for either.", :event/verification "clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 26 tests / 69 assertions, 0 failures both times (also fixed a hardcoded jurisdiction-count assertion in the pre-existing coverage-reporting test, 3 -> 4). Citation verification: the Clean Air Conservation Act Art. 23 citation could not be confirmed against its primary source directly -- law.go.kr/elaw.klri.re.kr's viewer is a JS SPA this iteration's tools could not render (the same class of limitation hit for Azerbaijan's e-qanun.az and Albania's qbz.gov.al in iterations 4/5) -- so it rests on multiple independent WebSearch-surfaced secondary sources instead of a direct fetch, consistent with how those prior iterations handled the same limitation. The Occupational Safety and Health Act citation is HIGHER confidence: WebFetch itself got HTTP 403 on the official ILO NATLEX-hosted English-translation PDF, but curl with a standard user-agent succeeded (200, real 10-page PDF), and its actual Article 36/80 text was extracted directly via pdftotext and read, not taken from a summary. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-1910-kor-coke-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1910/merges, commit 22abc4394f32a4351cd2ab951b05a6e22a2cf8b4) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 97d35f2bf6a9 -> 22abc4394f32 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None new this iteration (the 8-of-70 spec-basis classification pass itself is the main new finding, not a per-repo screen-out) -- see event/action for the classification method and the resulting candidate list: isic-1410/1420/1430/1512/3020 remain as genuine, not-yet-attempted real-world-ingest-gap targets for future iterations, pre-screened as real per-jurisdiction citation catalogs (unlike the false positives found in iterations 1/5).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- axis alternation is now 3 prod-ready / 3 real-world-ingest-gap across 6 iterations, evenly balanced.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 6, :event/at "2026-07-21T09:10:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 7, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1420", :event/action "Added United Kingdom (:GBR) as a 4th jurisdiction to fur.facts/catalog (was USA/ITA/CAN), one of the 5 pre-screened genuine candidates identified in iteration 6's spec-basis classification pass. GBR is a genuinely different shape from the other three jurisdictions: alongside labeling, the UK prohibits domestic fur farming outright (a production-side ban), so it gets its own honestly-named :fur-farming-prohibition key rather than being force-fit into the :fur-labeling/:species-sourcing shape USA/CAN use. Citations: Fur Farming (Prohibition) Act 2000 c.33 s.1 (Offences relating to fur farming, in force since 1 January 2003); Regulation (EU) No 1007/2011 Article 12 (non-textile-animal-origin labeling) -- the SAME regulation :ITA's entry already cites, confirmed still current as UK retained EU law post-Brexit rather than assumed superseded.", :event/verification "clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 35 tests / 118 assertions, 0 failures both times (this repo's existing tests already used >= count checks rather than hardcoded equality, so no pre-existing assertion needed fixing this time, unlike iteration 6). Both citations WebFetch-verified directly against legislation.gov.uk (The National Archives' official UK legislation site) -- no secondary-source fallback needed this iteration, a cleaner verification than iterations 4/5/6's e-qanun.az/qbz.gov.al/law.go.kr JS-SPA limitations. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-1420-gbr-fur-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1420/merges, commit 8a4b5345faff96472629e7e2ff04c5e2f5339f23) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 2955559f4ee0 -> 8a4b5345faff (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (target was pre-screened in iteration 6's classification pass).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- deliberately kept the pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis (direct edit, no background agent needed) rather than another ~25-30min agent-delegated stub-scaffold, using up the pre-screened candidate list from iteration 6. Remaining pre-screened, not-yet-attempted candidates: isic-1410 (apparel), isic-1430 (knitwear), isic-1512 (luggage), isic-3020 (railway rolling stock manufacturing). Axis alternation is now 3 prod-ready / 4 real-world-ingest-gap across 7 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 7, :event/at "2026-07-21T09:30:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 8, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-arm", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Armenia (ARM) from a pure blueprint-only stub, same pattern as iterations 2/4/5. Delivered: marketentry.facts (ARMEPS/armeps.am under the Ministry of Finance per the Law on Procurement (16 Dec 2016) -- specifically verified the law's own named 'bulletin' domain, procurement.am, is now dead/superseded rather than assuming armeps.am was the only candidate; TIN/registration investigated as one act performed by the Agency for the State Register of Legal Persons (Ministry of Justice), not the tax authority, on the strength of the State Revenue Committee's own OECD submission; an ineligible-bidders-list flagship check reusing Azerbaijan's boolean-registry-membership shape for an EXPLICIT, disclosed reason rather than default) + statute.facts (Civil Code, Labour Code, Personal Data Protection Law, and a Law on Limited Liability Companies -- confirming a 4th distinct commercial-entity-law structural pattern for this family: Armenia splits company law into per-entity-type standalone statutes, unlike BGR/DEU's single Commerce Act or AZE's Civil-Code-embedded provisions) + a real, disclosed scope-narrowing decision: a tax-arrears de-minimis provision structurally similar to Bulgaria's was found and read directly in the primary law text, but deliberately NOT used as the flagship check because a 2025 secondary source's own enumeration of current exclusion grounds omits it while confirming an unrelated amendment elsewhere in the same article -- i.e. real evidence the law changed since 2016 -- and Armenia's parliament.am was unreachable (TCP reset) to confirm one way or the other, so the possibly-repealed provision was left out rather than risked.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session: (1) spot-checked citation URLs live -- armeps.am (HTTP 200, self-identifying HTML), arlis.am Labour/Civil Code pages (302->200 redirect to canonical URLs, content-confirmed 'LABOUR CODE' title), moj.am register page (200); independently re-downloaded and pdftotext-verified both PDF-sourced citations myself (Law on Limited Liability Companies from translation-centre.am, Personal Data Protection Law from moj.am) -- both opened with the exact claimed 'LAW OF THE REPUBLIC OF ARMENIA, Adopted on [date]' text; independently re-checked procurement.am and confirmed it is genuinely dead (unreachable), corroborating the agent's dead-bulletin-domain finding; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked orgs/kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 33 tests / 108 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 10 warnings, matching exactly; (4) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-arm checkout was untouched before merging. Landed via server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-arm/merges, commit d6c4a9eb3c811fa1bb8f7a516617c84298bb6bfb) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced daed61e5ba57 -> d6c4a9eb3c81 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- 4 pre-screened candidates from iteration 6 remain queued (isic-1410/1430/1512/3020). Axis alternation is now 4 prod-ready / 4 real-world-ingest-gap across 8 iterations, evenly balanced.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 8, :event/at "2026-07-21T10:45:00Z"}
