{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 12, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-ben", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Benin (BEN) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a prior, unrelated Wave-1 initiative had already added a src/culture domain -- left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10. Delivered: marketentry.facts (investigated, rather than assumed, which body operates the e-procurement portal -- found ARMP (Autorité de Régulation des Marchés Publics, Loi N°2020-26 Art. 17-19) regulates/adjudicates but does NOT operate SIGMAP/marches-publics.bj, which is instead run by a separate body, the Direction Nationale de Contrôle des Marchés Publics (DNCMP), per the Code's own implementing décret -- a genuinely different ARMP-regulates/DNCMP-operates institutional split not seen in any prior sibling; the one-act-vs-two-act business/tax question resolved to a THIRD distinct variant -- two separate acts (RCCM registration + IFU issuance) by two separate authorities under two separate legal bases, filed together through one guichet-unique intake, unlike ALB/ARM/AZE's single-authority one-act model or ATG's sequential-prerequisite two-act model; a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE -- Art. 77 al.3's mandatory 5% MPME bid-evaluation price-adjustment margin, independently recomputed as a bid-EVALUATION adjustment rather than an eligibility gate, unlike every prior sibling's gate-shaped checks) + statute.facts (OHADA AUSCGIE company law, Code du Travail, Code du Numérique/APDP data-protection law) + honest scope-narrowing (rep-spec-basis nil -- Benin's Art. 61/62 exclusions extend to consortium members/subcontractors, a differently-scoped provision from a bidder's own representatives, so not force-fit; Art. 75's discretionary up-to-15%-community-preference and Art. 77's discretionary subcontracting-based margin both left unmodeled).", :event/verification "Independentl