nuinely no drift at all, i.e. their local checkout IS current and they really do lack a facts.cljc) were not further investigated this iteration -- those are more likely to be genuine '*ops'-architecture non-candidates per iteration 17's finding, but this was not re-confirmed at scale. isic-3812's own pre-existing test bug was found but not fixed (out of scope, flagged for a future iteration). Axis alternation is now 9 prod-ready / 10 real-world-ingest-gap across 19 iterations (this iteration counted as one batch despite touching 9 repos, since no new citation-writing was involved -- unlike every individual-jurisdiction-citation iteration before it).", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 19, :event/at "2026-07-21T19:40:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 20, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-bhs", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Bahamas (BHS) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a pre-existing src/culture domain from an unrelated prior Wave-1 initiative was left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/14/16/18. Delegated to a fresh background agent (isolated standalone clone) with an explicit research+verify+scaffold+push-to-branch-only mandate. Delivered: marketentry.facts (found the Bahamas' OWN four-part procurement structure -- Public Procurement Department + Chief Procurement Officer + Public Procurement Board + decentralised procurement units, all established by the Public Procurement Act, 2021, then RE-ENACTED with the SAME four parts by the Public Procurement Act, 2023 which ADDED a fifth institution absent from the 2021 Act: a dedicated Challenges and Appeal Tribunal (Part V) plus a Debarment Procedure part (Part VI) -- a genuinely new 'incumbent structure gains an oversight layer at re-enactment' finding, distinct from every prior sibling's split/non-split shape; found the Bahamas levies NO general income tax, so replaced every prior sibling's single TIN-style tax-identity check with a BIFURCATED pair -- an UNCONDITIONAL universal Business Licence Act, 2023 requirement plus a CONDITIONAL, threshold-gated VAT Act, 2014 registration (B$100,000 turnover threshold), both administered by the same Department of Inland Revenue but triggered independently, implemented as two separate governor checks; found a Registrar of Companies Act, 2024 already enacted to carve business registration out of the Registrar General's Department into a new standalone office, but its commencement is conditional on a future Ministerial Gazette notice and this session's live fetch of the Registrar General's own site showed no sign the transition has actually happened nearly two