{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 21, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-7820", :event/action "Queried the committed manifest/itonami-fleet-audit.edn for isic repos with the :facts-citations ingest-signal AND real-world-ingest-gap? true (i.e. repos that already have a facts.cljc, but score 0 on the https?:// URL-counting heuristic) not yet touched by any prior iteration -- found 62, most in the isic-0111..1312 range already known to be the agriculture/food-processing 'internal reference data, not a citation catalog' false-positive family. Sampled the non-agriculture remainder (machinery_repair/isic-3312, electronicrepair/isic-3313, itsupport/isic-6209, staffing/isic-7820, bizsupport/isic-8299) and found isic-8299's bizsupport.facts is a global-standards-body certification catalog (HIPAA/PCI-DSS/SOC2/GDPR/ISO-27001) -- real, but organized by standard rather than by jurisdiction, a genuinely different (not falsifiable) shape this loop's 'add a jurisdiction' pattern doesn't fit. isic-7820's staffing.facts, by contrast, IS a genuine per-jurisdiction tenure-cap/wage-compliance catalog (USA I-9/FLSA, Japan's Worker Dispatching Act + Minimum Wage Act, Germany's AÜG, UK's Agency Workers Regulations 2010) that scores 0 purely because every existing citation is a plain-text law name/section, not a URL -- the SAME documented metric-design-limitation already found for gas.facts/steam.facts before iterations 1/3 fixed those by adding a URL-bearing entry. Added France (:fra) as a 5th jurisdiction: Code du travail Art. L1251-12-1, the 18-month default cap on a contrat de mission's total duration.", :event/verification "This iteration specifically investigated, rather than took at face value, WHICH French Code du travail article actually states the numeric tenure cap today: initial WebSearch results pointed at Art. L1251-12, but WebFetch-reading that article's own current text (post-2018 'Ordonnances Macron' reform) directly 