tions independently verified before writing: WebFetch-confirmed the Umweltbundesamt's (Federal Environment Agency) own English page describing the BImSchG's permit framework and TA Luft's role, then specifically searched for and WebFetch-read the actual Anhang 1 zur 4. BImSchV text at gesetze-im-internet.de (Germany's official law portal, Bundesministerium der Justiz) and confirmed Item 1.11's exact wording naming 'Kokereien' -- not inferred from the generic law, the specific installation-type entry was read directly. Arbeitsschutzgesetz confirmed the same way -- official title, §3 and §5 headings read directly at gesetze-im-internet.de. clojure -M:test run directly in the child repo checkout before and after the edit: 27 tests / 75 assertions, 0 failures both times. Landed via throwaway branch itonami-loop/isic-1910-deu-coke-facts -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1910/merges, commit afb6f545dcf5190b6d1ec791e4ca27986dbdfbad) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 22abc4394f32 -> afb6f545dcf5 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "machinery_repair (isic-3312), electronicrepair (isic-3313) -- operations-coordination shape, no citation concept. itsupport (isic-6209) -- certification-standards catalog organized by standard not jurisdiction. cofog-03.2's firerisk domain sampled as a representative of the small cofog/unspsc/gtin families -- same operations-coordination shape, no facts.cljc at all.", :event/not-done-this-iteration "The isic real-world-ingest-gap classification work from iterations 6/17/19/21/23 combined has now covered: the original 8-candidate spec-basis pre-screen (exhausted iterations 1/3/6/9/11/13/15), the 185-repo :none-measured pin-staleness scan (iteration 19, 10 found/9 fixed), and the 62-repo :facts-citations-gap-but-scores-zero bucket (iteration 21/23, exhausted -- all non-agriculture candidates screened, all agriculture-range ones already documented as false positives from prior iterations). A future real-world-ingest-gap iteration will need either a genuinely fresh classification pass (the agriculture-range ~55 repos were never individually re-sampled, only pattern-matched) or should extend the classification method to a family outside isic entirely. Axis alternation is now 11 prod-ready / 12 real-world-ingest-gap across 23 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 23, :event/at "2026-07-21T23:05:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 24, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-blr", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Belarus (BLR) from a src/marketentry-and-src/statute-absent stub (a pre-existing src/culture domain from an unrelated prior Wave-1 initiative was left untouched), same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/14/16/18/20/22. Delivered: marketentry.facts (found a genuinely new THREE-WAY split -- one policy regulator (MART, Ministry of Antimonopoly Regulation and Trade, confirmed via MART's own official pravo.by clarification citing its Art. 10 powers) plus TWO separately-authorized, independently-branded e-procurement platform operators (RUE National Export Promotion Centre running goszakupki.by/icetrade.by/gias.by, and the Belarusian Universal Commodity Exchange running zakupki.butb.by) -- a shape distinct from a prior sibling's two-institutions-sharing-one-portal structure; a genuinely new TWO-ACT business/tax registration finding -- state registration (executive-committee justice directorate, under Presidential Decree No. 1) and UNP/tax registration (Ministry of Taxes and Duties, automatic and founder-passive within 5 working days) are legally separate acts by separate bodies, unlike a prior sibling's single simultaneous act; investigated rather than assumed whether Decree No. 1 (2009) is still current and found the honest answer is 'yes, but not for much longer' -- its own gazette metadata shows it loses legal force from 2027-07-01, with a replacement Law already visible in Belarus's own Bank of Draft Laws, a live illustration of this jurisdiction's characteristic Decree-to-Act-of-Parliament transition pattern; added a new business-registration-spec-basis accessor to the shared schema, mirroring a prior sibling's precedent of extending it when a jurisdiction's own institutional shape needs a slot no prior sibling required) + statute.facts (Civil Code -- confirmed Belarus has no standalone Commerce Code, the Civil Code itself supplies corporate-governance provisions, mirroring a prior sibling's finding; Labour Code; a 2021 Personal Data Protection Law). rep-spec-basis deliberately left nil after not finding comparably strong evidence of a personal-exclusion-grounds provision for Belarus specifically.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session (not merely re-reading the agent's report): (1) fresh standalone clone confirmed the diff touches exactly the 18 intended files and src/culture + test/culture are byte-identical to main (empty diff); (2) independently re-fetched and confirmed all three statute.facts citations verbatim against etalonline.by (Civil Code's law number/dates via WebFetch; Labour Code's law number/adoption/approval dates and its most recent 2025 amendment via curl+pandoc; Data Protection Law's law number and title via curl+pandoc); independently confirmed MART's own pravo.by news post cites its Art. 10 powers verbatim, confirmed BUTB's own page states its E-procurement-platform authorization verbatim (curl with a full browser user-agent succeeded where a bare curl hit an anti-bot JS challenge), confirmed MART's government activity page discusses public procurement, and independently confirmed Presidential Decree No. 1's own gazette metadata shows the exact 'утрата силы с 01.07.2027' (loses force from 2027-07-01) sunset clause verbatim; could NOT independently re-confirm NCMPS's own specific claim about operating goszakupki.by/icetrade.by/gias.by this pass -- curl hit an anti-bot JS fingerprinting challenge, WebFetch hit a TLS certificate error, and this session's WebSearch budget was exhausted -- noted honestly as unconfirmed-by-me due to tooling limits rather than treated as a red flag, given every other citation in this scaffold checked out precisely; (3) independently reconstructed the `:local/root` relative-path layout and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 35 tests / 114 ass